     "transcript": [
      {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 6.0,
       "text": "Before you seat people or split them into teams, there is a smaller question:",
       "sceneId": "p-chats"
      },
      {
       "start": 6.0,
       "end": 8.4,
       "text": "who is closest to whom?",
       "sceneId": "p-chats"
      },
      {
       "start": 11.95,
       "end": 16.972,
       "text": "Count shared group chats, and your closest person is… the boss.",
       "sceneId": "p-count"
      },
      {
       "start": 17.41,
       "end": 24.21,
       "text": "A chip has the same problem: thousands of cells. Which two belong side by side?",
       "sceneId": "p-chip"
      },
      {
       "start": 24.21,
       "end": 30.11,
       "text": "So first, give every pair a score: the higher it is, the closer they belong.",
       "sceneId": "p-chip"
      },
      {
       "start": 37.0,
       "end": 43.4,
       "text": "The first way: a pair's score is the weight of the wire between them.",
       "sceneId": "p-direct"
      },
      {
       "start": 43.4,
       "end": 50.0,
       "text": "A–B and D–E both score 5: ties go by name, whatever the input order.",
       "sceneId": "p-direct"
      },
      {
       "start": 51.18,
       "end": 56.647,
       "text": "B and D share no wire: by the first rule, nothing in common.",
       "sceneId": "p-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 56.647,
       "end": 62.713,
       "text": "Both are wired to C, and a link through C is only as strong as its weaker wire:",
       "sceneId": "p-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 62.713,
       "end": 65.958,
       "text": "min(4, 2) = 2.",
       "sceneId": "p-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 66.08,
       "end": 71.102,
       "text": "Check every pair: all 10 score, B–D included.",
       "sceneId": "p-list"
      },
      {
       "start": 71.3,
       "end": 74.5,
       "text": "Take a guess: which pair is closest?",
       "sceneId": "p-predict"
      },
      {
       "start": 74.5,
       "end": 79.744,
       "text": "X–Y has the thickest wire, 5; each triangle edge is only 4.",
       "sceneId": "p-predict"
      },
      {
       "start": 80.16,
       "end": 84.071,
       "text": "By direct wires, the first pair is X–Y;",
       "sceneId": "p-flip"
      },
      {
       "start": 84.071,
       "end": 88.871,
       "text": "by shared neighbours, P–Q = 4 + 4 = 8 moves ahead.",
       "sceneId": "p-flip"
      },
      {
       "start": 89.0,
       "end": 95.578,
       "text": "Both answers are right: one asks how thick a wire is, the other how tight a group is.",
       "sceneId": "p-models"
      },
      {
       "start": 97.19,
       "end": 100.19,
       "text": "Remember the boss?",
       "sceneId": "p-boss"
      },
      {
       "start": 102.5,
       "end": 109.744,
       "text": "One five-person chat ties ten pairs at once, so it says little about any one of them.",
       "sceneId": "p-dilute"
      },
      {
       "start": 109.744,
       "end": 117.011,
       "text": "So share each chat out: in a five-person chat each pair gets 1/4; a private chat gives a whole 1.",
       "sceneId": "p-dilute"
      },
      {
       "start": 117.14,
       "end": 120.607,
       "text": "Counted this way, your closest is Lin.",
       "sceneId": "p-rank"
      },
      {
       "start": 120.8,
       "end": 128.267,
       "text": "Clock and reset nets reach thousands of cells: unshared, every pair looks equally close.",
       "sceneId": "p-netlist"
      },
      {
       "start": 128.267,
       "end": 133.956,
       "text": "In the original tiny netlist: A–B gets 0.5, E–F gets 1.",
       "sceneId": "p-netlist"
      },
      {
       "start": 134.16,
       "end": 140.56,
       "text": "A score only decides who merges first; the merging itself starts in the next module.",
       "sceneId": "p-pipeline"
      },
      {
       "start": 141.5,
       "end": 147.5,
       "text": "The same pair of cells gets a different score under a different rule.",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 147.5,
       "end": 155.5,
       "text": "Affinity is not a distance and not a probability: it is a ranking under one model.",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 155.5,
       "end": 162.5,
       "text": "Next time someone says “we are the closest”, you can ask:",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 162.5,
       "end": 168.5,
       "text": "by which score?",
       "sceneId": "p-outro"
      },
      {
       "start": 170.6,
       "end": 176.6,
       "text": "In the lab below, change one wire's weight and watch the ranking move.",
       "sceneId": "p-end"
      }
     ],
