     "transcript": [
      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 7.756,
       "text": "Step one of clustering: which pairs belong together?",
       "sceneId": "k01-question"
      },
      {
       "start": 7.756,
       "end": 12.356,
       "text": "Give every pair a score, then rank them from high to low.",
       "sceneId": "k01-question"
      },
      {
       "start": 12.356,
       "end": 16.489,
       "text": "Note: a score ranks pairs; it does not group them.",
       "sceneId": "k01-question"
      },
      {
       "start": 16.889,
       "end": 22.356,
       "text": "One: direct weight. The score is the weight of the wire.",
       "sceneId": "k02-edge"
      },
      {
       "start": 22.356,
       "end": 26.044,
       "text": "G01's six edges give six pairs.",
       "sceneId": "k02-edge"
      },
      {
       "start": 26.044,
       "end": 33.289,
       "text": "A–B and D–E tie at 5: sorted by (−score, u, v), A–B comes first.",
       "sceneId": "k02-edge"
      },
      {
       "start": 33.689,
       "end": 36.489,
       "text": "Two: shared neighbours.",
       "sceneId": "k03-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 36.489,
       "end": 39.289,
       "text": "A–C: the direct wire is 1.",
       "sceneId": "k03-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 39.289,
       "end": 45.867,
       "text": "Add the link through B, at its weaker wire: min(5, 4) = 4.",
       "sceneId": "k03-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 45.867,
       "end": 47.667,
       "text": "Total: 5.",
       "sceneId": "k03-shared"
      },
      {
       "start": 48.067,
       "end": 50.867,
       "text": "B and D share no wire,",
       "sceneId": "k04-bd"
      },
      {
       "start": 50.867,
       "end": 55.444,
       "text": "but through C they get min(4, 2) = 2.",
       "sceneId": "k04-bd"
      },
      {
       "start": 55.444,
       "end": 61.133,
       "text": "So check all 10 pairs: a pair with no wire can still score.",
       "sceneId": "k04-bd"
      },
      {
       "start": 61.533,
       "end": 68.333,
       "text": "Change the score and the first pair changes. Look at the original author's priority graph.",
       "sceneId": "k05-priority"
      },
      {
       "start": 68.333,
       "end": 72.244,
       "text": "Direct weight: X–Y = 5 comes first.",
       "sceneId": "k05-priority"
      },
      {
       "start": 72.244,
       "end": 77.933,
       "text": "Shared neighbours: P–Q = 4 + 4 = 8 overtakes X–Y.",
       "sceneId": "k05-priority"
      },
      {
       "start": 78.333,
       "end": 86.022,
       "text": "Three, for multi-pin nets: two wide 5-pin nets and one private net.",
       "sceneId": "k06-pin"
      },
      {
       "start": 86.022,
       "end": 89.933,
       "text": "Share each net out over |e| − 1.",
       "sceneId": "k06-pin"
      },
      {
       "start": 89.933,
       "end": 95.844,
       "text": "A–B gets only 1/4 + 1/4 = 0.5; E–F gets 1.",
       "sceneId": "k06-pin"
      },
      {
       "start": 96.244,
       "end": 98.378,
       "text": "Four things to keep.",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 98.378,
       "end": 101.044,
       "text": "It ranks; it does not group;",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 101.044,
       "end": 103.644,
       "text": "the ranking must be stable;",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      },
      {
       "start": 103.644,
       "end": 111.511,
       "text": "a different score can pick a different first pair, and a score is not a distance. Try it in the lab below.",
       "sceneId": "k07-take"
      }
     ],
     "readingViolations": 0,
     "bytes": 4790219
    }
