     "transcript": [
      {
       "start": 3.4,
       "end": 5.8,
       "text": "The three scores again.",
       "sceneId": "a01-recap"
      },
      {
       "start": 5.8,
       "end": 11.044,
       "text": "Each one assumes something about which links count.",
       "sceneId": "a01-recap"
      },
      {
       "start": 11.444,
       "end": 18.467,
       "text": "U and V share no wire; both touch X: U–X is 10, V–X only 1.",
       "sceneId": "a02-min"
      },
      {
       "start": 18.467,
       "end": 22.6,
       "text": "Take the weaker wire: the link through X is 1.",
       "sceneId": "a02-min"
      },
      {
       "start": 22.6,
       "end": 28.956,
       "text": "With a sum it would be 11, and look almost as close as U–X itself.",
       "sceneId": "a02-min"
      },
      {
       "start": 28.956,
       "end": 35.533,
       "text": "V barely touches X. A chain is as strong as its weakest link.",
       "sceneId": "a02-min"
      },
      {
       "start": 35.933,
       "end": 44.511,
       "text": "Now a hub: H reaches six leaves at weight 3; nearby, P–Q share a real wire of weight 2.",
       "sceneId": "a03-hub"
      },
      {
       "start": 44.511,
       "end": 50.422,
       "text": "No two leaves are wired, yet each pair gets 3 through H: 15 pairs in all.",
       "sceneId": "a03-hub"
      },
      {
       "start": 50.422,
       "end": 55.089,
       "text": "Every one of them ranks above P–Q, which really are wired.",
       "sceneId": "a03-hub"
      },
      {
       "start": 55.089,
       "end": 61.622,
       "text": "This is a known weakness of shared neighbours; a common fix is to normalise by degree.",
       "sceneId": "a03-hub"
      },
      {
       "start": 62.022,
       "end": 68.022,
       "text": "Cost: with ten thousand cells, there are almost fifty million unordered pairs.",
       "sceneId": "a04-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 68.022,
       "end": 73.822,
       "text": "Enumerating along neighbours takes under sixty thousand steps on this grid.",
       "sceneId": "a04-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 73.822,
       "end": 79.511,
       "text": "Because a pair that scores has either a wire or a shared neighbour.",
       "sceneId": "a04-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 79.511,
       "end": 87.644,
       "text": "But one huge net alone brings hundreds of thousands of pairs, so many tools treat such nets separately.",
       "sceneId": "a04-cost"
      },
      {
       "start": 88.044,
       "end": 93.289,
       "text": "Why does pin-count divide by |e| − 1?",
       "sceneId": "a05-conserve"
      },
      {
       "start": 93.289,
       "end": 97.2,
       "text": "Add up the score each cell receives:",
       "sceneId": "a05-conserve"
      },
      {
       "start": 97.2,
       "end": 106.889,
       "text": "it equals the total weight of the cell's nets. Whatever its size, a net gives each pin exactly w(e).",
       "sceneId": "a05-conserve"
      },
      {
       "start": 107.289,
       "end": 109.422,
       "text": "Last, ties.",
       "sceneId": "a06-ties"
      },
      {
       "start": 109.422,
       "end": 114.556,
       "text": "Feed the nodes and edges in reverse and the ranking is identical.",
       "sceneId": "a06-ties"
      },
      {
       "start": 114.556,
       "end": 122.622,
       "text": "It matters: the next module merges the top pair first, and without a tie rule the result is not reproducible.",
       "sceneId": "a06-ties"
      },
      {
       "start": 123.022,
       "end": 130.933,
       "text": "Once the top pair A–B merges, the next comparison is no longer between two cells but between clusters.",
       "sceneId": "a07-clusters"
      },
      {
       "start": 130.933,
       "end": 135.511,
       "text": "AB and C share two wires: 1 + 4 = 5.",
       "sceneId": "a07-clusters"
      },
      {
       "start": 135.511,
       "end": 141.711,
       "text": "Add up the wires between two clusters: that is the affinity the next module uses.",
       "sceneId": "a07-clusters"
      },
      {
       "start": 142.111,
       "end": 144.178,
       "text": "Six things to keep.",
       "sceneId": "a08-summary"
      },
      {
       "start": 157.178,
       "end": 162.244,
       "text": "Next: merging for real, with the summed weight between clusters.",
       "sceneId": "a08-summary"
      }
     ],
     "readingViolations": 0,
     "bytes": 7058630
    }
